pic", "title": "Cultural humility", "children": [{"id": "07622a89-b374-4eae-8ad4-812e1849afa3", "type": "concept", "title": "Lifelong learning and critical self-reflection"}, {"id": "adb2ac52-408a-4132-8c99-c622454ce264", "type": "concept", "title": "Power imbalance and institutional accountability"}, {"id": "2a7dfc18-c33a-4c5a-9f3e-360a2ff6c79c", "type": "concept", "title": "Repair, apology, and growth-oriented practice"}], "description": "Students distinguish humility from a checklist approach to culture."}, {"id": "5e537226-c7d9-4ee0-8e70-dd2fb5c97bd5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Implicit bias and privilege", "children": [{"id": "dfc07caf-eb09-4acc-af0a-2ba976e0f077", "type": "concept", "title": "Implicit associations and expectation effects"}, {"id": "807a311c-34b6-452c-a221-05c7b95f8d58", "type": "concept", "title": "Privilege, normalization, and invisibility"}, {"id": "3e436ad7-24e9-4894-94d6-c32dd5a4d9e1", "type": "concept", "title": "Bias interruption routines"}], "description": "Students study bias as a professional responsibility and a design problem, not just an individual flaw."}]}, {"id": "e2c1e1ca-e4ac-4363-b4bc-8d2aaa7c4f6c", "type": "topic", "title": "Race, Ethnicity, Language, and Schooling", "description": "This unit examines how race, ethnicity, and language shape educational opportunity, identity, curriculum, discipline, placement, and achievement. Students learn to move from awareness to anti-racist and linguistically sustaining practice.", "children": [{"id": "c11aaaeb-4bd5-4842-bb94-adc97ee73a04", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Race and racism in education", "children": [{"id": "de683371-1d2d-451b-9747-be5ce4078a77", "type": "concept", "title": "Racialization and schooling history"}, {"id": "4679f030-d451-46dc-a27d-3591f0eed65d", "type": "concept", "title": "Disproportionality in discipline and special education"}, {"id": "7256f685-5b83-48ee-9d66-75f45ca09899", "type": "concept", "title": "Anti-racist classroom and school routines"}], "description": "Students analyze racism as interpersonal, institutional, historical, and curricular."}, {"id": "18878e82-e90f-4d87-8f93-e40de35e51e0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethnicity, immigration, and belonging", "children": [{"id": "2d3684b0-9e58-42f8-a464-c0ae5c904d23", "type": "concept", "title": "Immigrant and refugee experiences"}, {"id": "a9854c94-673c-49db-9b3a-c3e975048fcd", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethnic identity development"}, {"id": "8c214c58-e645-4d5b-9898-af353768704c", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding tokenism and cultural essentialism"}], "description": "Students learn to support students whose cultural identities, migration histories, and family experiences shape school life."}, {"id": "29871ad3-42ed-4b91-8dba-bbf65f6f0931", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Language and multilingual learners", "children": [{"id": "6826737b-78f4-4c2d-be57-7046d9d19ef6", "type": "concept", "title": "Translanguaging and home-language assets"}, {"id": "4f585283-9b54-4b4e-8676-8a27d2ca48d2", "type": "concept", "title": "English learner identification and support"}, {"id": "2285e121-cea0-41ff-9a00-c84ba54983ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Language access for families"}], "description": "Students study language as an asset and a civil-rights issue."}]}, {"id": "b3bbf421-7aeb-4cdf-b074-0c76f6609257", "type": "topic", "title": "Gender, Sexuality, Religion, and Safe Learning Environments", "description": "Students need classrooms where identity is not a liability. This unit prepares educators to create respectful environments across gender, sexuality, and religion while navigating professional, legal, and community contexts.", "children": [{"id": "63cafa3c-ce59-4c3e-8d7b-6fc113fc450b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gender and schooling", "children": [{"id": "49ca4e0b-93d7-42e4-acf4-c5670fcf8d7d", "type": "concept", "title": "Gender stereotypes and hidden curriculum"}, {"id": "9569dd7a-6061-4452-b0b0-7262790534f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Gender-expansive students"}, {"id": "c994d810-52f1-4245-bb9b-9f4e3e7dd9dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Equitable participation and feedback patterns"}], "description": "Students examine how gender norms shape participation, expectations, curriculum, and belonging."}, {"id": "c173bcb6-3f93-47e0-a3ac-1ea869f310c6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "LGBTQ+ inclusive education", "children": [{"id": "6691c7b4-91d6-4d6d-af1f-112a638800da", "type": "concept", "title": "Names, pronouns, and privacy"}, {"id": "60b4a090-e149-42c8-b5bd-8c8093eb4775", "type": "concept", "title": "Inclusive texts and examples"}, {"id": "967be508-6433-4c1e-ad2d-1fbd30222c3b", "type": "concept", "title": "Anti-bullying and harassment response"}], "description": "Students learn classroom practices that support safety, dignity, and accurate representation."}, {"id": "074c9bd7-5dc9-4bcd-99f4-720c16ff5a84", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Religion and worldview diversity", "children": [{"id": "dce4842f-6cb6-4e4a-96a3-99e653f9ab58", "type": "concept", "title": "Religious literacy and constitutional boundaries"}, {"id": "5c2bef29-8117-444a-847c-89e0729cfcea", "type": "concept", "title": "Holidays, dress, diet, and observance"}, {"id": "213f051a-630e-462a-b5a1-508845d1e9a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Dialogue across difference"}], "description": "Students learn to address religion respectfully in public-school contexts."}]}, {"id": "fde6dd5b-234b-4cac-9368-f3c8dc58e31e", "type": "topic", "title": "Socioeconomic Inequality, Opportunity Gaps, and Community Context", "description": "This unit helps students interpret achievement differences as opportunity differences shaped by resources, policies, neighborhoods, and institutional design rather than student deficits.", "children": [{"id": "083e24b4-d623-4222-8111-08515e276fca", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Class and educational opportunity", "children": [{"id": "f6a903dd-e18f-47d6-aa51-c7b5acf73b69", "type": "concept", "title": "Poverty, housing, food security, and attendance"}, {