, and build critical literacy without reducing culture to celebration.", "children": [{"id": "cff28ded-d1cd-4c60-be75-9210bd8094db", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Representation and curriculum audit", "children": [{"id": "382516c2-7c47-491a-b274-7f7b33120783", "type": "concept", "title": "Mirrors, windows, and sliding glass doors"}, {"id": "f14e7ab8-c850-4ccd-906c-c270ad72daab", "type": "concept", "title": "Tokenism and stereotypes"}, {"id": "02f1518f-c30a-48d7-ad22-79afd14c142c", "type": "concept", "title": "Curriculum mapping for representation and power"}], "description": "Students learn to examine whose stories, expertise, and perspectives appear in curriculum."}, {"id": "dfe9f5e5-e1c2-44f0-8abc-19094d373d5c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Counter-narratives and people's history", "children": [{"id": "1e5d1ade-e2d2-41e0-bec7-dc72021ea06e", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary sources and local histories"}, {"id": "1cd186a1-6520-4eef-bd08-8b625ced2401", "type": "concept", "title": "Multiple perspectives and contested narratives"}, {"id": "f5d185e2-57c7-4fe3-b798-14fe4b4a56a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Student inquiry into justice and change"}], "description": "Students learn how alternative sources deepen historical and civic understanding."}, {"id": "f8a30413-4033-435f-9d1c-4d6d1bd635ba", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critical media and information literacy", "children": [{"id": "88badbc2-b7f6-46d1-8ba8-9c36a33ed3e8", "type": "concept", "title": "Source evaluation and misinformation"}, {"id": "adfb3fba-d6b9-490a-96da-9c63282db2c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Visual and digital representation"}, {"id": "4fa99979-c862-4edf-8d10-8b751561a27c", "type": "concept", "title": "Bias, framing, and civic dialogue"}], "description": "Students learn to help students evaluate media, algorithms, and public discourse."}]}, {"id": "1037f87f-e2dc-482d-837d-ddaad2e92987", "type": "topic", "title": "Inclusive Classroom Climate, Restorative Practice, and Belonging", "description": "Equity lives in daily classroom routines. This unit focuses on relationship-centered practice, community building, discipline equity, and restorative responses that maintain dignity and accountability.", "children": [{"id": "32659419-f204-4db6-ac6c-09fe72c1db8d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Belonging and classroom culture", "children": [{"id": "022fe62b-76d9-40dc-aad8-e133837f805e", "type": "concept", "title": "Community agreements and norms"}, {"id": "4d651bed-c896-4385-a43b-6c0642658598", "type": "concept", "title": "Student voice and co-creation"}, {"id": "a99576af-3c84-4d30-83bb-c9856bbea89d", "type": "concept", "title": "Belonging surveys and climate checks"}], "description": "Students learn to design routines that communicate safety, respect, and high expectations."}, {"id": "2f50759c-ca59-4483-8eb1-1278ba1931d6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Restorative and culturally affirming practices", "children": [{"id": "d92bd1fe-4fc1-48d4-8b18-a87e48d13179", "type": "concept", "title": "Restorative circles and conferences"}, {"id": "078b55a0-84ae-401a-b3e7-d9749ff431fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Accountability without humiliation"}, {"id": "50f46448-fad2-4f0e-892a-8fe7171a80e2", "type": "concept", "title": "Culturally responsive classroom management"}], "description": "Students learn alternatives to exclusionary discipline that repair harm and sustain community."}, {"id": "8e38fc71-d994-4e83-91c5-9613d3a5d73a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Trauma-informed and healing-centered practice", "children": [{"id": "95904e57-aeaf-4d77-9d9c-39fc71dd2928", "type": "concept", "title": "Predictability, choice, and regulation"}, {"id": "c6e82326-0b89-4dfa-837b-141f680371b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding pathologizing students"}, {"id": "55527c17-93fe-4456-829b-cb89b7333860", "type": "concept", "title": "Referral, boundaries, and educator care"}], "description": "Students learn how stress, trauma, and resilience intersect with identity and schooling."}]}, {"id": "296dd6f7-c566-4c5b-b950-a28f47c09359", "type": "topic", "title": "Family, Community, and Participatory Partnerships", "description": "Families and communities are not peripheral to learning. This unit prepares educators to build reciprocal partnerships that respect family expertise and share power.", "children": [{"id": "b86f0dc3-06b3-4d90-bd93-257321dd02a1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Family engagement as partnership", "children": [{"id": "188e56db-ed07-4d9d-b6a2-a4b46d61c335", "type": "concept", "title": "Two-way communication"}, {"id": "66ebb1f4-d984-4621-b68a-27800ac22fbc", "type": "concept", "title": "Strengths-based family narratives"}, {"id": "ec37586b-8185-4ad4-af74-4e40557e3bd3", "type": "concept", "title": "Conferences, home visits, and trust building"}], "description": "Students learn to move beyond compliance-oriented communication toward authentic relationship."}, {"id": "c62785d4-4965-4451-85ee-93f1e11d0dee", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Language access and cultural responsiveness", "children": [{"id": "55f347f9-394e-4b40-a5b2-12afbff7650a", "type": "concept", "title": "Interpretation and translation"}, {"id": "1d03c1af-277a-4352-9b39-333a9cad1a22", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding child-as-interpreter practices"}, {"id": "dbf7363e-f769-4508-89af-a532cf197643", "type": "concept", "title": "Culturally responsive meeting design"}], "description": "Students learn to make school communication accessible and respectful."}, {"id": "f347c997-15a1-4153-8236-5fd49f38647c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Community-based and participatory education", "children": [{"id": "66c7dfe1-19ee-4c9d-8951-ca2cb50ee1d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Community walks and asset mapping"}, {"id": "2441be02-da30-435c-a8a4-f4ab04ee653c", "type": "concept", "title": "Co-designed projects"}, {"id": "0f7da86e-e4b9-497e-be3c-6f90bf9fcfa6", "type": "concept", "title": "Youth and family voice in decision-making"}], "description": "Students learn to connect curriculum and improvement work to community priorities."}]}, {"id": "1766a90e-bc35-4998-b902-027653798f1c", "type": "topic", "title": "Civil Rights, Policy, Equity Data, and School Systems", "description": "Equity-centered educators need systems literacy. This unit introduces civil-rights obligations, data sources, and policy tools for identifying and addressing inequity beyond individual classrooms.", "children": [{"id": "4b421ffc-5f2c-428a-9ef2-8c6eaed7f6f4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Civil rights and legal context", "children": [{"id": "98c05a50-a2d1-4c3d-b07c-ed086becc2dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Title VI, Title IX, Section 504, ADA, and language access"}, {"id": "91fe66e5-5960-4ee1-99c9-69cab42d5a09", "type": "concept", "title": "Office for Civil Rights roles"}, {"id": "fc6ec602-122f-4c59-a9c9-5c43c8c2794d", "type": "concept", "title": "Nondiscrimination, harassment, and equal access"}], "description": "Students learn the basic federal protections that shape school responsibilities."}, {"id": "8c139c72-f9c4-4878-8697-f2fe52e2f92f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Equity data and disproportionality", "children": [{"id": "f673b475-fbb7-4019-bb6a-a9349673546c", "type": "concept", "title": "Civil Rights Data Collection"}, {"id": "2c32086c-ce83-4417-8337-aa7e09925201", "type": "concept", "title": "Discipline, course access, special education, and advanced opportunities"}, {"id": "17f4c84e-739b-4f4c-9f4c-2864fb9898e2", "type": "concept", "title": "Disaggregation, intersectionality, and small-number caution"}], "description": "Students learn to use data to ask better questions, not to label students or communities."}, {"id": "927ef84d-1da4-469c-a348-f0f6fcffe745", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Equity audits and improvement planning", "children": [{"id": "de18290f-b39b-4caa-8a85-c6df1dd08e4f", "type": "concept", "title": "Equity indicators and root-cause analysis"}, {"id": "aefa98cc-8b68-458d-9e31-401843a1fb48", "type": "concept", "title": "Stakeholder engagement"}, {"id": "b535a59a-f422-49de-9d0d-545a052d7e9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Monitoring outcomes and unintended consequences"}], "description": "Students learn how schools turn evidence into action."}]}, {"id": "c0138c08-69a2-4c96-9103-8ad6ebde7e64", "type": "topic", "title": "Teacher Leadership, Resistance, and Sustaining Equity Work", "description": "The capstone unit prepares students to sustain equity work as reflective professionals. Students learn to navigate resistance, build coalitions, measure progress, and keep students at the center.", "children": [{"id": "fdf71003-f4b7-438b-80d4-5a03143adc76", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Teacher leadership and coalition-building", "children": [{"id": "94022179-66a0-4767-81b8-c8c693bb7507", "type": "concept", "title": "Professional learning communities"}, {"id": "f7f0991b-93f3-41b1-afc6-9a5662aec532", "type": "concept", "title": "Coaching and peer inquiry"}, {"id": "0efa7ede-b0a1-4f16-b465-4e3298fc4b15", "type": "concept", "title": "Distributed leadership and shared responsibility"}], "description": "Students learn how classroom educators influence teams, curriculum, policy, and culture."}, {"id": "79b6f506-2d8f-43d3-9625-6b8f83c156f3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Navigating conflict and resistance", "children": [{"id": "1f9a5651-12d4-41ce-aa92-02293ab549a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Facilitation across difference"}, {"id": "5867f47c-8059-4c4f-9e3c-43a8b543abc0", "type": "concept", "title": "Common resistance patterns"}, {"id": "61a9dce7-c0c8-44d2-a0b6-9e651b86822e", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical boundaries and professional communication"}], "description": "Students learn to respond to disagreement with clarity, evidence, humility, and courage."}, {"id": "46b23c99-05ab-4b51-92c0-506d2995e634", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sustaining practice and accountability", "children": [{"id": "beb6c0bb-6a99-4754-98d2-ec60cae956b9", "type": "concept", "title": "Equity-centered teaching artifacts"}, {"id": "61566e27-f5a7-4af1-b5b3-1543b39a2e7a", "type": "concept", "title": "Reflection and evidence of impact"}, {"id": "15ea6f46-c24b-4b16-8ce5-dc4e98edc59b", "type": "concept", "title": "Personal professional learning plan"}], "description": "Students build a portfolio that shows growth and a plan for continued learning."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$demejson$::jsonb,
  true,
